schema: nodx/0.1
type: document
id: print-landscape-dashboard
title: Operations Dashboard — Landscape Print Sheet
subtitle: Wide tables, generous spacing, A3 landscape
language: en
dir: ltr
authors: [NODX Working Group]
created: 2026-05-10
keywords: [print, landscape, dashboard, spacing, padding]
requires: [rich-tables, style]
---

:::style
@page {
  size: A3 landscape;
  margin: 16mm 18mm 16mm 18mm;
}
@page :first {
  margin-top: 26mm;
}

body { font-family: "Source Sans Pro", system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; color: #1f2937; }

h1 { font-size: 28pt; margin: 0 0 8pt; padding-bottom: 6pt; border-bottom: 0.8pt solid #0f766e; color: #0f172a; }
h2 { font-size: 16pt; margin: 18pt 0 8pt; color: #0f172a; padding-inline-start: 8pt; border-inline-start: 4pt solid #0f766e; }

.kpi-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
  gap: 12pt;
  margin: 8pt 0 18pt;
}
.kpi-grid > div {
  padding: 14pt 16pt;
  background-color: #ecfdf5;
  border: 0.4pt solid #0f766e;
  border-radius: 6pt;
}
.kpi-grid h3 {
  margin: 0 0 6pt;
  font-size: 9.5pt;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  color: #475569;
  font-weight: 600;
}
.kpi-grid .value {
  font-size: 28pt;
  font-weight: 700;
  color: #0f766e;
  margin: 0;
}
.kpi-grid .delta {
  font-size: 10pt;
  color: #475569;
  margin: 2pt 0 0;
}

table {
  border-collapse: collapse;
  width: 100%;
  margin: 8pt 0 16pt;
  page-break-inside: avoid;
}
th, td {
  border: 0.4pt solid #cbd5e1;
  padding: 8pt 12pt;
  vertical-align: top;
  text-align: start;
}
th {
  background-color: #0f172a;
  color: #f8fafc;
  font-weight: 600;
  letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  font-size: 9.5pt;
}
tr:nth-child(even) td {
  background-color: #f8fafc;
}

.legend {
  margin: 6pt 0 18pt;
  font-size: 9.5pt;
  color: #475569;
  display: flex;
  gap: 18pt;
  padding: 8pt 12pt;
  background-color: #f1f5f9;
  border-radius: 4pt;
}
.legend strong { color: #0f172a; }

aside {
  margin: 12pt 0;
  padding: 12pt 16pt;
  border-inline-start: 4pt solid #b45309;
  background-color: #fffbea;
  border-radius: 4pt;
  page-break-inside: avoid;
}

footer {
  margin-top: 24pt;
  padding-top: 8pt;
  border-top: 0.4pt solid #94a3b8;
  font-size: 9pt;
  color: #64748b;
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
}
::: style

# Operations Dashboard — Landscape Print Sheet {#title}

The landscape orientation gives wide tables more room to breathe and lets
high-density indicator grids fit on a single page. Padding and spacing values
are deliberately larger than the portrait report so the page reads well from
across a meeting table.

::::section {#kpis}
## Quarterly Indicators {#kpis-heading}

:::note {type="info"}
The four cards below use a CSS grid (`grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr)`)
with `gap: 12pt`. Print engines that ignore CSS Grid fall back to vertical
stacking, which still reads correctly.
::: note

[Latency p95, error rate, deploy frequency, change-failure rate.]

| Indicator | Value | Target | Status |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Latency p95 (ms) | 184 | < 200 | OK |
| Error rate (%) | 0.27 | < 1.00 | OK |
| Deploy frequency (per week) | 23 | > 15 | OK |
| Change-failure rate (%) | 6.4 | < 10.0 | OK |
| Mean time to recovery (min) | 18 | < 30 | OK |
:::: section

::::section {#regions}
## Regional Breakdown {#regions-heading}

| Region | Latency p95 | Error rate | Active deploys | On-call | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| EU-West | 178 ms | 0.21 % | 8 | 2 engineers | Stable, no incidents in Q1 |
| EU-Central | 192 ms | 0.34 % | 6 | 1 engineer | Watching DB latency tails |
| US-East | 165 ms | 0.18 % | 9 | 3 engineers | Stable |
| US-West | 201 ms | 0.42 % | 7 | 2 engineers | Latency improvement plan filed |
| AP-Southeast | 268 ms | 0.61 % | 4 | 1 engineer | Edge-cache rollout in Q2 |

:::note {type="warning"}
Regions with latency above the 250 ms threshold trigger the **edge-cache
rollout** workflow. AP-Southeast is currently the only region above threshold.
::: note
:::: section

::::section {#legend}
## Legend And Notation {#legend-heading}

[**Indicator**: a measurable property of the system. **Target**: the contractual
threshold from the SLO catalogue. **Status**: OK if value meets target,
ATTN otherwise. Values are computed over a 28-day rolling window.]
:::: section

::::section {#footer}
## Distribution

This sheet is intended for printing at A3 landscape. When printed at A4 it
remains legible thanks to the page-break-inside: avoid hint on tables and
callouts. Send a sealed PDF copy to the operations leads and archive a packaged
`.nodx` in the compliance vault.
:::: section
